== Campaign ==
[[Kemi Badenoch]] visited Croydon before launching the Conservatives local election campaign in March 2026, and stated that [[shoplifting]] would be a major issue.<ref>{{cite news |last=Cecil |first=Nicholas |date=19 March 2026|title=Croydon crime put at heart of Tory local election campaign for England by Badenoch |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/politics/crime-croydon-london-conservatives-local-election-campaign-kemi-badenoch-b1275628.html |access-date=29 March 2026|work=The Standard }}</ref>

On 28 March, [[Nigel Farage]] held a rally at [[Fairfield Halls]].<ref>{{cite AV media |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/tv/news/nigel-farage-heckled-reform-uk-london-b2947726.html |title=Farage repeatedly heckled at Reform UK event in London |date=28 March 2026 |access-date=29 March 2026|work=The Independent}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|date=29 March 2026|title=Reform UK launches London election campaign in Croydon |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9vly297yk1o |access-date=30 March 2026|publisher=BBC News|first=Susana|last=Mendonça }}</ref> He announced that [[Reform UK]] would cut [[council tax]] and said there were 21 council officers on salaries above £100,000, despite the [[debt crisis]].<ref>{{cite news|first1=Nicholas|last1=Cecil|first2=Rachael|last2=Burford |date=27 March 2026|title=Farage's Reform takes on Tories in furious election battle for Croydon |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/politics/nigel-farage-reform-local-elections-london-crime-conservatives-labour-greens-b1276627.html |access-date=29 March 2026 |work=The Standard}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Oluwalana |first=Ayokunle |date=29 March 2026|title=Nigel Farage heckled at Croydon Reform UK rally in sweary rant |url=https://www.mylondon.news/news/south-london-news/nigel-farage-heckled-croydon-reform-33679294 |access-date=29 March 2026|work=My London}}</ref>

In early 2025, the local Reform branch selected Sharon Carby, a person from [[Bradford]] who died in 2024, as their mayoral candidate.<ref>{{cite web |date=27 August 2025|title=Farage party picked a dead woman to run for Croydon Mayor |url=https://insidecroydon.com/2025/08/27/farage-party-picked-a-dead-woman-to-run-for-croydon-mayor/ |access-date=29 March 2026|first=Walter|last=Cronxite |work=Inside Croydon}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=6 September 2025|title=Reform UK in Chaos as Party Selects Woman Who Had Been Dead For Six Months as Mayoral Candidate |url=https://dorseteye.com/reform-uk-in-chaos-as-party-selects-woman-who-had-been-dead-for-six-months-as-mayoral-candidate/ |access-date=29 March 2026 |work=Dorset Eye }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Lawton |first=Jerry |date=28 August 2025|title=Nigel Farage’s Reform UK select woman to run for mayor but 'make grave mistake' |url=https://www.dailystar.co.uk/news/politics/nigel-farages-reform-uk-select-35810955 |access-date=29 March 2026|work=Daily Star}}</ref>

